<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is Partnership to Pvt Ltd Conversion?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>Partnership to Pvt Ltd conversion is the statutory re-registration under Section 366 of the Companies Act, 2013. All property, rights, and interests vest in the new company (Section 367). All debts and obligations remain binding (Section 368). Legal proceedings continue uninterrupted (Section 370). Business continues as going concern &ndash; no gap in operations.</p>
                    <p>Tax-neutral under Section 47(xiii): no capital gains if same proportions, 5-year share holding, 50% minimum. For <a href="/statutory-audit">Statutory Audit</a> (mandatory post-conversion), see our page. For <a href="/fdi-compliance">FDI Compliance</a> with foreign shareholders, see our page.</p>
                    <p>Addresses the gap between traditional partnership and modern requirements: institutional banking, equity funding, ESOP, corporate governance. For <a href="/private-limited-company-registration">Pvt Ltd Registration</a> (fresh incorporation), see our page.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Partnership to Pvt Ltd:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Section 366:</strong> Registration of partnership firm as company &ndash; main conversion provision</li>
                        <li><strong>Section 47(xiii):</strong> IT Act &ndash; capital gains exempt (same proportions, 5-year holding, 50% minimum)</li>
                        <li><strong>URC-1:</strong> Conversion application &ndash; filed linked with SPICe+ Part B</li>
                        <li><strong>URC-2:</strong> Newspaper advertisement &ndash; 21 clear days in English + Marathi</li>
                        <li><strong>Section 367:</strong> All property and rights of firm vest in new company</li>
                        <li><strong>Section 115BAA:</strong> Concessional 22% corporate tax rate &ndash; lower than 30% partnership rate</li>
                    </ul>

                </div>
            </div>
